#====================================================================
# DRAFT-mesa-24.3.4-meson-proc-self-exe-feature-macro
# OpenHarmony 适配: 用构建系统注入能力宏替代源码 OHOS 条件编译宏
# (getprogname/program_invocation_name -> /proc/self/exe)
# 触发事件: mesa 24.3.4 HarmonyOS PC 适配 (R02/R04 审查返工, PR #7521)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-mesa-24.3.4-meson-proc-self-exe-feature-macro
trigger_tool:           meson|clang|conan
phase:                  build|testing
error_signature:        util_get_process_name|process_test|__OHOS__|__OHOS_FAMILY__|getprogname not available|program_invocation_name

severity:               2
category:               compat, ohos, libc, build-system
match_keywords:         getprogname, program_invocation_name, proc/self/exe, __OHOS__, feature macro, meson, readlink, HAVE_READ_PROC_SELF_EXE, HAVE_PROC_SELF_EXE
title:                  Inject a build-system capability macro instead of an OHOS source macro for proc/self/exe process name

root_cause:             OHOS musl libc lacks program_invocation_name/getprogname but provides /proc/self/exe; a source-level __OHOS__ guard binds platform adaptation to an uncontrolled macro definition and violates rule R8 (no OHOS conditional-compilation macros in source/patches).

rec_approach:           portability-patch
rec_description:         In meson.build, gate on host_machine.system() == 'harmonyos' (or an equivalent build-system platform check) to inject a platform-independent capability macro (e.g. HAVE_READ_PROC_SELF_EXE); in C source, branch only on that capability macro and use readlink("/proc/self/exe") as a POSIX fallback. Never reference __OHOS__/__OHOS_FAMILY__ in source or patches.
rec_command:            If cc.has_header_symbol('errno.h','program_invocation_name', args:'-D_GNU_SOURCE'): pre_args += '-DHAVE_PROGRAM_INVOCATION_NAME'.  If not that && host_machine.system()=='harmonyos': pre_args += '-DHAVE_READ_PROC_SELF_EXE'

forbid_1_pattern:        __OHOS__|__OHOS_FAMILY__.*readlink|#ifdef __OHOS__
forbid_1_reason:         Platform-specific source macros hide the actual POSIX capability and violate R8.
forbid_1_consequence:    Platform adaptation silently depends on an externally-defined macro; a different libc can pick the wrong branch.

doc_file:                 knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-mesa-24.3.4-meson-proc-self-exe-feature-macro.md
last_updated:             2026-09-02
source_event:             mesa/24.3.4 HarmonyOS PC adaptation, review rework R02/R04, PR #7521
draft:                    true
contributor_id:           8B28
source_pr:                7521
source_commit:            96b2fb963ffe26dcdec320d7c7d07bc1d4ed0dfe
patches_referenced:       patches/0002-meson.build.patch, patches/0006-src-util-u_process.c.patch
verification_cmd:         ninja -C <build> src/util/process_test src/gallium/tests/trivial/ohos_adapt_test && GALLIUM_PIPE_SEARCH_DIR=<build>/src/gallium/targets/pipe-loader <build>/src/gallium/tests/trivial/ohos_adapt_test
verification_exit:        0
verification_log:         archives/m/mesa/24.3.4/reports/r02-evidence-adaptation-validation.log (及 R02/R04 证据日志)
verification_evidence:    process_test exit 0; ohos_adapt_test "[OHOS] PASS: process name matches binary basename" + "OHOS_ADAPT_TEST: ALL PASS"; patches __OHOS__ count 0
valeus_scope:             OHOS/HarmonyOS aarch64 C/C++ libraries needing process-name/libc capability fallback; Meson (or equivalent) builds
limits:                  Not for platforms that already have program_invocation_name/getprogname; pure-CMake projects need an equivalent capability-macro mechanism

metrics_success_count:    1
metrics_fail_count:       0
metrics_confidence:       0.9
metrics_last_used:        2026-09-02